name tank-radius-clean-1
timeout 32000

# THE RANGE MISSION, CLEAN HALF — the control for tank-radius-tanks.fbm. Identical in every line except
# the two `set store` lines: same spawn, same leg, same altitude, same commanded speed, same internal
# fuel. What differs is the jet, so the difference between the two runs IS what the tank is worth.
#
# WHY `set fuel_int_pct` AND NOT `set fuel_pct`. `fuel_pct` distributes over EVERY tank the model
# declares, and the pinned f16 declares four — two internal (3,486 lb each) and two EXTERNAL
# (2,991 lb each). `set fuel_pct 100` therefore fuels a clean jet with 12,954 lb, of which 5,982 lb sit
# in containers it is not carrying (doc/modules/stores.md §Gaps 3, measured on cmd-avionics.fbm).
# `fuel_int_pct 100` fills only the tanks no pylon is plumbed to: 6,972 lb, the internal load, and the
# first time this tree could declare a clean jet at all.
#
# THE MEASUREMENT is a straight, level cruise leg flown until the fuel is gone: the last telemetry row
# and the ground distance from the spawn point to it. The waypoint is deliberately further away than
# the jet can reach, so nothing about the profile changes when the range does.
#
# READING RULE: the exit code is NOT the measurement — a jet that runs its tanks dry at cruise altitude
# ends as a `FBFlightMonitor` KO, which is exit 2 and is the CORRECT outcome for this file. The
# measurement is the distance and the endurance in the last telemetry row. Read beside
# tank-radius-tanks.fbm; alone this file proves nothing.

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.00000 8000 90.0 400       # 8,000 m ASL, due east, 400 KCAS
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100                       # 6,972 lb internal, external tanks EMPTY
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  wp 46.90000 75.00000 8000 400              # ~5,200 km: further than any fuel state here reaches
